# Nexus PM Integration
# Copy to .env.local and fill in your values
NEXUS_API_URL=https://your-nexus-project.supabase.co/functions/v1
NEXUS_API_KEY=your-shared-secret-key-here

# Nexus task creation (task-api). Separate credential from NEXUS_API_KEY above, which only
# authenticates the Nexus `users` lookup (Authorization: Bearer). Task creation authenticates with
# an `x-api-key` issued in Nexus (api_keys row with tasks:write AND tasks:read). Nexus requires the key to be
# scoped to a DEPARTMENT or a SPRINT (never neither); use a department-scoped, sprint-less key whose department
# has task-status definitions. The key's scope places the task. NEXUS_TASK_API_URL defaults to ${NEXUS_API_URL}/task-api.
#
# Required shape of NEXUS_TASK_API_KEY (created in the Nexus UI; server-side only, never in browser code):
#   permissions = tasks:write + tasks:read      (read is needed by TIMEOUT_UNKNOWN reconciliation)
#   scope       = DEPARTMENT                    (Nexus requires a department OR a sprint scope on every key)
#   Sprint scope = NOT required                 Sprint / Team membership = NOT required
# OPERATOR CONFIGURATION REQUIRED: the key's department owns every task Rock Solid creates, and that department
# MUST have active task statuses (Nexus rejects task creation with a 500 when it has none; Admin, Media, ORS,
# PFCC and Pastors do, General and Programs do not). Nothing in this repo chooses the department.
# Assignment is direct: rocksolid_admin_mappings.nexus_user_id -> task assignee_id.
NEXUS_TASK_API_URL=https://your-nexus-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/task-api
NEXUS_TASK_API_KEY=your-nexus-task-api-key-here
